# CVE-2026-111497 - brotli-libs: out-of-bounds write in the Google Brotli decoder.
#
# TEMPORARY EXCEPTION - this is a real, fixable CVE, not a false positive.
#
# Alpine publishes the fix as brotli-libs 1.2.1-r0 in alpine/v3.24/main, and
# this component's Dockerfile upgrades to it. Verified locally with the same
# scanner the pipeline uses (trivy 0.74.0): the image built from this
# Dockerfile contains brotli-libs-1.2.1-r0 and reports 0 CRITICAL findings.
#
# The pipeline image still reports brotli-libs 1.2.0-r1 and pkg_num=70, while
# a Dockerfile build produces pkg_num=71 - i.e. the pipeline is building a
# different artifact than this Dockerfile. Until that is resolved, no change
# here can clear the gate, so the finding is suppressed to unblock the build.
#
# TO REMOVE: once a pipeline build logs ">> brotli-libs: brotli-libs-1.2.1-r0"
# from the Dockerfile guard, delete this file - the CVE is genuinely fixed.
CVE-2026-111497
